    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1048">

                <pb facs="1293" n="1275" xml:id="pg1275"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">833.24/8–2146</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chief of the Division of Lend-Lease and Surplus
                        Property Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Havlik</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to Mr. Robert W. Cavanaugh, Treasury
                    Department</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-21">August 21, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Cavanaugh</hi>: It has been brought to my
                    attention that the Treasury Department, Lend-Lease Fiscal Operations, recently
                    received a payment of $1,300,000 from the Embassy of Uruguay on lend-lease
                    account.</p>
                <p>Since this was an overpayment and since there appears to be no possibility that
                    any further payment will become due under the terms of the Lend-Lease Agreement
                    with Uruguay, it is the view of the State Department that any further payment or
                    payments by Uruguay which may be offered should not be accepted by this
                    Government. In the event that any further payment is offered the matter should
                    be referred to my office.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hubert</hi> F. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Havlik</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
